# LEARNINGS - incident intake (schema template)

Append-only. One row per incident. Every incident becomes exactly one bounded rule with one
canonical home and one named enforcement surface; a row missing any field is invalid. This
template carries the fixed columns and an empty state; it contains no live rows. Gate that reads
it: `scripts/protean-ops/check-learnings.py`. No preference, and no lesson without an enforcement
surface, is accepted.

## Columns (fixed)

| column | meaning |
|---|---|
| learning id | `lrn-<n>`, sequential |
| incident | what happened, one sentence |
| root cause | the mechanism behind it, one sentence |
| one bounded rule | the single rule the incident yields (imperative, testable) |
| canonical home | the one file that owns the rule; every other mention is a pointer |
| enforcement surface | the gate or check that rejects a violation, by exact command or gate id |
| independent verifier | the role that verifies it without authoring the fix |
| status | `open (enforcement pending)`, `enforced`, or `superseded <by>` |
| evidence path | where the incident is documented on disk |

